    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 239\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6684, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  criminal procedure law, in relation to the\n      payment of certain fines and mandatory surcharges\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend Criminal Procedure Law to provide  that  payment\nof  court  imposed  fines  would  take  priority  over  payment of State\nmandated surcharges for  Vehicle  and  Traffic  Law,  drug,  or  alcohol\noffenses.  This  bill  intends to ensure increased funds are received by\ncounty STOP-DWI Programs, which continue to  receive  fewer  funds  each\nyear under the current funding scheme.\n \n  The STOP-DWI Program is entirely supported by court imposed fines from\nalcohol  and drug-related vehicle offenses. While this funding mechanism\nwas sufficient when the program began, over time  additional  fines  and\nsurcharges  have  been created, pushing the STOP-DWI Program further and\nfurther down on the list of  recipients.  Compounding  this  issue,  the\nsignificant  decrease in alcohol and drug-related offense convictions we\nhave enjoyed in recent years has  come  at  a  price  for  the  STOP-DWI\nProgram.\n \n  I recognize both the importance of the STOP-DWI Program and the fiscal\ntroubles it now faces. Still, this bill was passed without consideration\nof  its  fiscal  impact  upon existing programs. If signed into law, the\nresult would be a direct offsetting reduction to  the  State's  Criminal\nJustice Improvement Account, funds of which go directly to crime victims\nthrough the Victim Assistance Program.\n \n  While  I  support  the intent of the bill and recognize the problem it\nattempts to address,  the  appropriate  remedy  cannot  involve  harming\nanother  population  in need of our help. I applaud the STOP-DWI Program\nfor the impact it has had upon our State and I am willing to  work  with\nthe  Legislature  to  address  the  program's fiscal concerns during the\nupcoming budget process. For these reasons, I  am  constrained  to  veto\nthis bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
